# Earth Jukebox: NASA Space Apps 2026

Click a real natural event on a 3D NASA map and hear it. Live data from NASA EONET and USGS,
sound made in the browser with Tone.js, no backend needed.

## Run it
    python3 -m http.server 8000
    # open http://localhost:8000/jukebox.html

## Events and sounds
| Event | Sound idea | Data |
|---|---|---|
| Wildfires | crackling pops + low roar | EONET |
| Storms | wind whoosh + water plinks, pitch by wind speed | EONET |
| Volcanoes | deep boom, pitch by latitude | EONET |
| Floods | soft sine drops | EONET |
| Landslides | low rumble | EONET |
| Earthquakes (new) | thud + rumble, lower/louder = bigger magnitude | USGS M4.5+ |
| Drought (new) | dry crackles + thin hot breeze | EONET |
| Dust & Haze (new) | wide sandy breath | EONET |
| Sea & Lake Ice (new) | glassy bell tones | EONET |
| Snow (new) | quiet floating plinks | EONET |
| Heat & Cold (new) | warm drone, thinner at high latitude | EONET |

## Credits
NASA EONET, NASA GIBS imagery, USGS Earthquake feed, Three.js, Tone.js.